<title>CHINA: China sets import tariff raw sugar, feed, cocoa.</title>
<headline>China sets import tariff raw sugar, feed, cocoa.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's customs authorities announced temporary import tariffs for 1997 on a list of items on Friday, setting the tariff on raw cane sugar at 12 percent compared with the official rate of 30 percent.</p>
<p>It set the temporary 1997 tariff on made-up animal feeds at five percent compared with the official rate of nine percent, the International Business Daily said.</p>
<p>It set the temporary tariff on cocoa beans at 10 percent compared with the official rate of 20 percent, the newspaper said. The temporary tariff on cocoa butter was set at 15 percent compared with the official rate of 45 percent.</p>
</text>
